# Build context for every repo-root build: build-docker.sh (devel, full-devel,
# full, lite), run-demo.sh and scale-test-dod-mission.sh (base, inspector,
# evaluation, dod demo + peer, C node).
#
# Patterns here are anchored at THIS directory, so a bare name like `deploy/`
# matches only ./deploy -- never examples/*/deploy, which the dod images do copy.
# .dockerignore is read from the context root only: builds whose context is
# src/ or src/autonomous-trust/ use the .dockerignore in those directories.
# Note that a `#` comment must own its whole line; trailing text is part of the
# pattern.

**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.tox/
.git/
.tilt/
*.egg-info/
# node_modules is reinstalled inside the inspector Dockerfile's builder stage;
# keep the ~200MB host tree out of the build context.
**/node_modules/

# --- Large host-only trees ------------------------------------------------
# Nothing below is read by any build: checked against every COPY/ADD source and
# every `RUN --mount=source=` in the repo. Together these are ~31GB of a ~33GB
# context that was being streamed and cached on every build.
#
# embedded/ is the 15G buildroot tree (the Dockerfiles inside it are
# buildroot's own, never built by our scripts); .scale-results/ is 13G of
# scale-test output; deploy/ is 2.3G of runtime assets that are bind-mounted at
# run time rather than built in.
embedded/
.scale-results/
deploy/
.minikube/
.demo-state/
attic/

# --- Host build/venv artifacts --------------------------------------------
**/.venv/
**/.rustup/
**/.pytest_cache/
# src/c/build* rides along inside `COPY src/c` (Dockerfile-c, Dockerfile-native,
# Dockerfile.zta) but is never read -- those builds cmake fresh into their own
# dir, and two of them already `rm -rf` the stale examples/build they inherit.
src/c/build/
src/c/build-*/
# Copied by Dockerfile-native/-devel as part of `COPY src/autonomous-trust/rust`,
# then rebuilt: the image installs its own rustup, so host artifacts never hit.
**/rust/target/
# Where build-docker.sh's run_builder() parks .venv/.tox/node_modules/.rustup
# while conda-build walks a package dir. Normally empty by the time any build
# runs, but a killed run can strand ~1.3GB there until the next reap.
src/.at-builder-stash/

# src/dist/conda-repo is deliberately NOT ignored -- src/Dockerfile mounts it
# (`RUN --mount=source=src/dist/conda-repo`), which reads the build context.
